//@version=6
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MTF Fractals + Stage · v6 · STRATEGY · calibrated for XAUUSD and BTCUSD
//
// Trading rules (see STRATEGY.md)
//   • Breakout entry: the chart-TF swing high (low) is Broken on the bar close
//     and the higher-TF bias is not against the trade (≥ "Min higher-TF bias").
//   • Flip-retest entry: the chart-TF level is in Flip retest and the bar closes
//     back on the broken side (old resistance holding as support, or the
//     reverse); one entry per level.
//   • Stop: entry − 1.5 × chart ATR (or the structure level ± buffer).
//     Target: 2 R. Stop to breakeven at +1 R. Optional ATR trail, time stop, and
//     exit when the opposite chart-TF swing breaks.
//   • Position size: risk % of equity ÷ stop distance, so every trade risks the
//     same fraction of the account on gold and on bitcoin alike.
//   • No entries in the gold rollover window, outside the trading session, or
//     outside the backtest range. Orders fill on the signal bar's close
//     (process_orders_on_close), the same bar the indicator's alerts fire on.
//   The indicator part below is identical to mtf_fractals_stage_v6.pine.
//
// What it does
//   • Williams fractals (swing highs / swing lows) on the chart TF and on
//     5s / 10s / 15s / 30s / 1m / 5m / 15m / 1H / 4H / D / W. A row is shown
//     only when it is higher than the chart TF, so on a 1s chart every row is
//     available and the Chart row is the 1s row (nothing is lower than 1s);
//     on a 5m chart the rows are 15m and up. Right side strict, so a fractal
//     can never be broken on the bar that confirms it; equal extremes allowed
//     on the left (input) so double tops / bottoms at a tied price register.
//
// How to read the table (one row per timeframe)
//     Swing hi  – price of the last swing high of that TF (resistance)
//     Stage     – what price has done with that level since it printed
//     Swing lo  – price of the last swing low of that TF (support)
//     Bias      – +1 when the swing high is broken, −1 when the swing low is
//                 broken, 0 otherwise; the Σ row sums the enabled, visible rows
//     Hover a level for its ATR, retest band, break buffer and age; hover a
//     stage for what it means. Chart-row levels are also drawn as lines and
//     labelled on the right edge of the chart.
//   • The most recent fractal of each side on each TF gets a stage (the table
//     always shows the latest swing of each side, so a new fractal replaces the
//     previous level and restarts its stage at Confirmed):
//       Confirmed    – fractal confirmed on this TF's latest bar (Chart row with
//                      bar-close gating: also on the bar after; higher TFs: on the
//                      previous closed bar of that TF; in both cases the row
//                      shows Retest instead when the chart bar has left the band
//                      and is back in it)
//       Holding      – no close through the level yet; chart price is outside the
//                      retest band or has not left it since the fractal printed
//       Retest       – level intact, the chart bar's range reaches into the retest
//                      band after a bar has been entirely outside it at least once
//                      (also shown after a failed break)
//       Broken       – this TF's close went through the level by more than the
//                      break buffer; stays until this TF closes back through the
//                      level by the buffer (Failed break), the next fractal, or
//                      the level expires (Expire level input)
//       Flip retest  – level broken earlier, a chart bar has left the band and the
//                      current bar's range is back inside it (support ⇄ resistance)
//       Failed break – level was broken, then this TF's close went back through it
//                      by more than the break buffer; stays until the level is
//                      broken again or the next fractal (shows Retest whenever
//                      the chart bar is inside the band). A re-break fires the
//                      break alert again.
//   • Every higher-TF value (level, ATR, break state, age) comes from COMPLETED
//     bars of that TF ([1] offset + lookahead_on), so the table is identical on
//     history and in real time. Break / Failed break are judged on that TF's own
//     close; Retest / Flip retest use the live chart bar.
//   • The Chart row confirms fractals, updates its level and break state and
//     fires its fractal / break alerts only on the bar close (input), so they
//     cannot appear intrabar and vanish. Retest / Flip retest are range events
//     on every row and update live.
//   • Defaults differ from v5: every row is on (rows below the chart TF are
//     simply hidden), Weekly is on (the only higher-TF row a D chart can show),
//     and tied double tops / bottoms now print a fractal (input tieLeft).
//   • Bias (data window, table column, optional tint): +1 per enabled, visible
//     TF whose last swing high is Broken / Flip retest, −1 per TF whose last
//     swing low is Broken / Flip retest; intact levels, Retest and Failed break
//     count 0.
//     NOTE: opposite sign to the v5 script, which scored intact levels and so
//     read bearish on an upside breakout. Re-create anything built on the old
//     "MTF fractal bias" value.
//   • Rows whose TF is lower than the chart TF, equal to it, or not a whole
//     multiple of it are hidden (request.security cannot return them reliably);
//     the Σ row tooltip lists them. Tick charts hide all higher-TF rows and skip
//     the rollover filter.
//
// Calibration
//   Distances are measured in ATR(14) of the timeframe they belong to, so one
//   multiplier means the same thing on $4,000 gold and $80,000 bitcoin and on
//   5m as on D. The v5 fixed 0.15 % band equalled ~0.5 × ATR on 1H gold and was
//   far too tight on BTC and on D / W. Its fixed-percent width survives as
//   "Percent" mode; the stage logic above is the same in both modes.
//       retest band   ±0.50 × √(row ATR × chart ATR), never narrower than the
//                     break buffer   a pullback to the level, not every bar; on
//                     the Chart row this is 0.5 × ATR, and a D level seen from a
//                     5m chart gets a band a few 5m-ATRs wide instead of half a
//                     daily range
//       break buffer   0.15 × row ATR, floored at 0.012 % of the level (≈ $0.50
//                     on gold, one quiet-hours spread) so a close inside the
//                     spread never counts as Broken in thin sessions
//       fractal        2 / 2   Williams, right side strict; equal extremes on
//                              the left allowed (input; Off = the strict v5 test)
//   After ATR normalisation XAUUSD and BTCUSD need the same multipliers, so the
//   inputs apply to every symbol. The symbol profile ("Auto" detects it) sets
//   what genuinely differs: gold CFDs and COMEX halt 17:00–18:00 New York, so on
//   timeframes up to 1H the XAUUSD profile ignores fractals whose centre bar
//   opens in the 16:40–18:20 New York window (16:30–18:20 for 30m / 45m bars,
//   16:00–18:20 for 1H bars, so the bar that closes into the 17:00 halt is
//   always included; not on crypto venues, where tokenised gold and BTC trade
//   24/7); gold prints 2 decimals, BTC whole dollars.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
strategy("MTF Fractals + Stage v6 Strategy", shorttitle = "MTF Fractals Strat", overlay = true, pyramiding = 0, initial_capital = 10000, default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1, commission_type = strategy.commission.percent, commission_value = 0.03, slippage = 2, process_orders_on_close = true, max_lines_count = 50, max_labels_count = 50)

// ── Inputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
string G_PROF  = "Symbol profile"
string G_FRACT = "Fractal"
string G_STAGE = "Stage calibration"
string G_TF    = "Timeframes"
string G_DISP  = "Display"

profile = input.string("Auto", "Symbol profile", options = ["Auto", "XAUUSD", "BTCUSD", "Generic"], group = G_PROF,
     tooltip = "Auto detects XAU / GOLD / GC futures and BTC / XBT symbols. The profile only sets what differs between the markets: the gold rollover filter and the price format (gold 2 decimals, BTC whole dollars). All calibration inputs below apply to every profile.")

leftBars       = input.int(2, "Bars left",            minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_FRACT)
rightBars      = input.int(2, "Bars right (confirm)", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_FRACT)
tieLeft        = input.bool(true, "Allow equal highs / lows on the left side", group = G_FRACT,
     tooltip = "On: equal highs / lows are tolerated anywhere in the left window, so the newest bar of a plateau or of a tight double top / bottom tied to the tick registers as the fractal (looser than the built-in Williams Fractal, which caps the plateau at 4 bars). Off: strict on both sides, as in the v5 script, so a tied extreme never prints a fractal.")
rolloverMode   = input.string("Auto", "Ignore gold rollover-window fractals", options = ["Auto", "On", "Off"], group = G_FRACT,
     tooltip = "Gold CFDs and COMEX halt 17:00-18:00 New York; bars around the halt and the Sunday open print isolated extremes that are not tradable levels. On timeframes up to 1H, fractals whose centre bar opens in the 16:40-18:20 New York window are ignored (16:30-18:20 for 30m / 45m bars, 16:00-18:20 for 1H bars, so the bar that closes into the 17:00 halt is always included). Auto = on for the XAUUSD profile on venues that halt (not tokenised gold on crypto exchanges); bitcoin stays off. Select On if your feed halts in this window.")
chartCloseOnly = input.bool(true, "Chart-TF signals on bar close only", group = G_FRACT,
     tooltip = "On: the Chart row confirms a fractal, updates its level and its Broken / Failed break state, draws the mark and fires the 'Chart up/dn fractal' and 'Chart swing high/low broken' alerts only once the chart bar has closed (equivalent to 'Once per bar close'); Retest / Flip retest still follow the live bar range. Off: v5 behaviour, a fractal can be confirmed and a break judged intrabar, and both can vanish if the bar later moves. Higher-TF rows always use completed bars.")

bandMode   = input.string("ATR", "Band mode", options = ["ATR", "Percent"], group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "ATR: bands are multiples of ATR (recommended). Percent: band and buffer are a fixed % of the level on every timeframe (the v5 width); the retest and break logic is the same in both modes.")
atrLen     = input.int(14,    "ATR length",            minval = 2,    maxval = 100,              group = G_STAGE)
retestMul  = input.float(0.50, "Retest band (× ATR)",  minval = 0.05, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.05, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Multiplied by the geometric mean of the row's ATR and the chart ATR, so higher-TF bands shrink toward the chart's scale; never narrower than the row's break buffer. On the Chart row it is simply × ATR.")
breakMul   = input.float(0.15, "Break buffer (× ATR)", minval = 0.0,  maxval = 2.0, step = 0.05, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "This TF's close must exceed the level by this much (of the row's own ATR) to count as Broken, and must close back through it by the same amount for a Failed break.")
minBufPct  = input.float(0.012, "Min break buffer (% of level, ATR mode)", minval = 0.0, step = 0.002, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Floor under the ATR break buffer so a close inside the spread never counts as Broken when ATR collapses in thin sessions. 0.012 % ≈ $0.50 on $4,200 gold, ≈ $9 on $77,000 BTC (negligible next to its ATR buffer).")
retestPct  = input.float(0.15,  "Retest band % (Percent mode)",  minval = 0.01, step = 0.01,  group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Fixed % of the level for every row, so one value cannot fit every timeframe: 0.15 % is about half an hourly ATR on gold (the v5 setting), a tenth of a daily ATR, and on BTC about half of that again. Roughly 0.3 % for BTC intraday and 0.5 % or more for daily levels. ATR mode scales this automatically.")
breakPct   = input.float(0.045, "Break buffer % (Percent mode)", minval = 0.0,  step = 0.005, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Fixed % of the level on every timeframe (3/10 of the Percent retest band, the same ratio as the ATR defaults). Set 0 for any close through the level to count (v5 had no buffer; Broken still stays until a Failed break or a new fractal).")
maxAge     = input.int(0, "Expire level N bars after confirmation (0 = never)", minval = 0, group = G_STAGE,
     tooltip = "Counted in bars of the level's own timeframe, starting at the bar that confirms the fractal; the level is removed on the Nth bar. The table tooltip shows age from the fractal's centre bar (for higher-TF rows, as of that TF's last completed bar), which is 'Bars right' larger.")

useChart = input.bool(true, "Chart TF", group = G_TF, inline = "tf0")
use5S    = input.bool(true, "5s",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf0")
use10S   = input.bool(true, "10s",      group = G_TF, inline = "tf0")
use15S   = input.bool(true, "15s",      group = G_TF, inline = "tf0")
use30S   = input.bool(true, "30s",      group = G_TF, inline = "tf0", tooltip = "Seconds rows appear only on seconds charts below them (1s chart: all four; 5s chart: 10s / 15s / 30s; 10s chart: 30s; 15s chart: 30s). On a 1s chart the Chart row is the 1s row: nothing is lower than 1s, so no separate 1s row exists. Seconds data needs a TradingView plan that offers seconds charts.")
use1     = input.bool(true, "1m",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf1")
use5     = input.bool(true, "5m",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf1")
use15    = input.bool(true, "15m",      group = G_TF, inline = "tf1", tooltip = "A row is shown only when its length is above the chart length and a whole multiple of it. 1m: on seconds charts. 5m: on 1m and seconds charts that divide 5 minutes (hidden on 2m / 3m / 4m). 15m: on 1m, 3m, 5m and such seconds charts (hidden on 2m, 4m, 10m). Hidden rows are summarised in the Σ row tooltip.")
use60    = input.bool(true, "1H",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf2")
use240   = input.bool(true, "4H",       group = G_TF, inline = "tf2")
useD     = input.bool(true, "Daily",    group = G_TF, inline = "tf2")
useW     = input.bool(true, "Weekly",   group = G_TF, inline = "tf2", tooltip = "1H: hidden on 45m charts. 4H: hidden on 45m and 3H charts. Weekly is the only higher-TF row available on a D chart and needs 'Bars left' + 'Bars right' + 1 completed weekly bars (5 with the defaults) before it can show a level. On seconds charts the loaded history is short, so D and W rows may say 'only N bars'.")

showMarks    = input.bool(true,  "Plot fractal marks",             group = G_DISP, inline = "marks")
bigMarks     = input.bool(true,  "large",                          group = G_DISP, inline = "marks", tooltip = "Triangle marks on confirmed chart-TF fractals: large (normal size) or small (tiny).")
showStageTbl = input.bool(true,  "Stage table",                    group = G_DISP)
showLabels   = input.bool(true,  "Labels on last chart fractals",  group = G_DISP)
showLines    = input.bool(true,  "Level lines (chart TF)",         group = G_DISP)
showHtfLines = input.bool(false, "Level lines (higher TFs)",       group = G_DISP)
showBiasBg   = input.bool(false, "Background tint from MTF bias",  group = G_DISP)
labelSize    = input.string("large",  "Label size",      options = ["small", "normal", "large", "huge"], group = G_DISP, inline = "size")
tblSize      = input.string("normal", "Table text size", options = ["tiny", "small", "normal", "large"], group = G_DISP, inline = "size")
tblPos       = input.string("top_right", "Table position", options = ["top_left", "top_right", "bottom_left", "bottom_right"], group = G_DISP)
bullCol      = input.color(color.new(color.teal, 0), "Bull", group = G_DISP, inline = "col")
bearCol      = input.color(color.new(color.red, 0),  "Bear", group = G_DISP, inline = "col")

// ── Profile resolution (all "simple" values: fixed for the whole run) ────────
string tick     = str.upper(syminfo.ticker)
string root     = str.upper(syminfo.root)
bool   isFut    = syminfo.type == "futures"
bool   isEq     = syminfo.type == "stock" or syminfo.type == "fund"
bool   symGold  = str.contains(tick, "XAU") or (str.contains(tick, "GOLD") and not isEq) or (isFut and (root == "GC" or root == "MGC"))
bool   symBtc   = ((str.startswith(tick, "BTC") or str.startswith(tick, "XBT")) and not isEq and not str.endswith(tick, ".D")) or (isFut and (root == "BTC" or root == "MBT"))
string resolved = profile == "Auto" ? (symGold ? "XAUUSD" : symBtc ? "BTCUSD" : "Generic") : profile
bool   isCrypto = syminfo.type == "crypto"
bool   rollOn   = rolloverMode == "On" or (rolloverMode == "Auto" and resolved == "XAUUSD" and not isCrypto)
// fmtPx only runs on the last bar, so close is the live price; a BTC-prefixed
// product priced below 1,000 (leveraged token, ETN) keeps its own tick format.
string pxFmt    = resolved == "XAUUSD" ? "0.00" : resolved == "BTCUSD" and close >= 1000 ? "0" : format.mintick
bool   useAtrBand = bandMode == "ATR"
int    chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.isticks ? "1" : timeframe.period)

// ── Band helpers (price units) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
breakBuf(float lvl, float atrV) =>
    useAtrBand ? math.max(breakMul * atrV, lvl * minBufPct / 100.0) : lvl * breakPct / 100.0

retestBand(float lvl, float bandAtr) =>
    useAtrBand ? retestMul * bandAtr : lvl * retestPct / 100.0

// ── Williams fractal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
isUpFractal() =>
    bool ok = bar_index >= leftBars + rightBars
    float mid = high[rightBars]
    if ok
        for i = 0 to leftBars + rightBars
            if i < rightBars and high[i] >= mid
                ok := false
            if i > rightBars and (tieLeft ? high[i] > mid : high[i] >= mid)
                ok := false
    ok

isDnFractal() =>
    bool ok = bar_index >= leftBars + rightBars
    float mid = low[rightBars]
    if ok
        for i = 0 to leftBars + rightBars
            if i < rightBars and low[i] <= mid
                ok := false
            if i > rightBars and (tieLeft ? low[i] < mid : low[i] <= mid)
                ok := false
    ok

// ── Per-TF level engine (runs inside each request.security context) ──────────
// Returns, for the bar `off` bars ago: the last fractal level of each side, this
// TF's ATR, whether a fractal confirmed on that bar, the age of each level in
// bars of this TF (from the fractal's centre bar), the open time of each
// fractal's centre bar, the break state of each level judged on this TF's own
// close (0 intact · 1 broken · 2 failed break), and how many bars this context
// has. off = 1 together with lookahead_on is the standard non-repainting
// higher-TF pattern. tfSec is the TF length in seconds, passed in so the
// rollover filter never depends on how timeframe.in_seconds() behaves inside a
// request. gate = false postpones both the fractal confirmation and the break /
// failed-break judgement (used by the Chart row to wait for the bar close);
// history is unaffected because every historical bar is confirmed.
tfEngine(simple int off, simple int tfSec, bool gate) =>
    float atrRma  = ta.atr(atrLen)
    float atrSeed = ta.cum(ta.tr(true)) / (bar_index + 1)   // expanding mean while the RMA warms up
    float atrV    = na(atrRma) ? atrSeed : atrRma
    int   nBars   = bar_index + 1
    // Window starts at the open of the bar that closes into the 17:00 halt:
    // 16:00 for 1H bars, 16:30 for 30m / 45m, 16:40 for 15m and below.
    string rollSess = tfSec >= 3600 ? "1600-1820:1234567" : tfSec >= 1800 ? "1630-1820:1234567" : "1640-1820:1234567"
    int   rollT   = na
    if rollOn and tfSec <= 3600 and not timeframe.isticks
        rollT := time(timeframe.period, rollSess, "America/New_York")
    bool  inRoll  = not na(rollT)
    bool  upNow   = isUpFractal() and not inRoll[rightBars] and gate
    bool  dnNow   = isDnFractal() and not inRoll[rightBars] and gate
    var float lastUp = na
    var float lastDn = na
    var int   upAge  = 0
    var int   dnAge  = 0
    var int   upT    = na
    var int   dnT    = na
    var int   upB    = 0
    var int   dnB    = 0
    if upNow
        lastUp := high[rightBars]
        upAge  := rightBars
        upT    := time[rightBars]
        upB    := 0
    else
        upAge += 1
    if dnNow
        lastDn := low[rightBars]
        dnAge  := rightBars
        dnT    := time[rightBars]
        dnB    := 0
    else
        dnAge += 1
    if maxAge > 0
        if upAge - rightBars >= maxAge
            lastUp := na
            upT    := na
            upB    := 0
        if dnAge - rightBars >= maxAge
            lastDn := na
            dnT    := na
            dnB    := 0
    if not upNow and not na(lastUp) and gate
        float bufUp = breakBuf(lastUp, atrV)
        if close > lastUp + bufUp
            upB := 1
        else if upB == 1 and close < lastUp - bufUp
            upB := 2
    if not dnNow and not na(lastDn) and gate
        float bufDn = breakBuf(lastDn, atrV)
        if close < lastDn - bufDn
            dnB := 1
        else if dnB == 1 and close > lastDn + bufDn
            dnB := 2
    [lastUp[off], lastDn[off], atrV[off], upNow[off], dnNow[off], upAge[off], dnAge[off], upT[off], dnT[off], upB[off], dnB[off], nBars[off]]

// ── Stage machine (chart side, one independent instance per call site) ───────
//   st     : 0 none · 1 Confirmed · 2 Retest · 3 Broken · 4 Holding · 5 Flip retest · 6 Failed break
//   bstate : break state from the engine (this TF's close vs level ± buffer)
//   armed  : after a break, a chart bar has been entirely outside the retest band at least once
//   away   : since the level printed, a chart bar has been entirely outside the band at least once (a break also counts)
//   t      : open time of the fractal's centre bar; a change means a new level
sideStage(float lvl, float atrV, float chartAtr, bool hit, int t, int bstate) =>
    var bool armed = false
    var bool away  = false
    bool fresh = not na(t) and (na(t[1]) or t != t[1])
    if fresh or na(lvl)
        armed := false
        away  := false
    int st = 0
    if not na(lvl)
        float buf  = breakBuf(lvl, atrV)
        float band = math.max(retestBand(lvl, math.sqrt(atrV * chartAtr)), buf)   // the near zone always covers the buffer zone
        bool near  = high >= lvl - band and low <= lvl + band                     // chart bar range reaches into the band
        bool newBreak = bstate == 1 and bstate[1] != 1
        if newBreak
            armed := false
        if bstate == 1 and not near
            armed := true
        if not near or bstate != 0
            away := true
        if bstate == 1
            st := armed and near ? 5 : 3
        else if bstate == 2
            st := near ? 2 : 6
        else if hit and not (near and away)
            st := 1
        else if near and away
            st := 2
        else
            st := 4
    st

stageName(int s) =>
    switch s
        1 => "Confirmed"
        2 => "Retest"
        3 => "Broken"
        4 => "Holding"
        5 => "Flip retest"
        6 => "Failed break"
        => "—"

stageColor(int s) =>
    switch s
        1 => color.yellow
        2 => color.orange
        3 => color.red
        4 => color.lime
        5 => color.fuchsia
        6 => color.gray
        => color.gray

// Plain-language meaning of each stage, shown in label and table tooltips.
stageDesc(int s) =>
    switch s
        1 => "Confirmed: the fractal has just been confirmed on this timeframe. The level is fresh and untested."
        2 => "Retest: the level is intact and the current chart bar reaches back into the retest band after having been away from it. Watch for rejection (level holds) or a close through it (break)."
        3 => "Broken: this timeframe closed through the level by more than the break buffer. A broken swing high counts +1 to the bias, a broken swing low −1."
        4 => "Holding: no close through the level yet and price is away from it (or has not left the band since the fractal printed)."
        5 => "Flip retest: the level was broken, price moved away and the current chart bar is back at it from the other side. The old resistance is being tested as support, or the old support as resistance."
        6 => "Failed break: the level was broken but this timeframe then closed back through it by more than the buffer. The break did not hold; the level is in play again."
        => "No level: no fractal of this side has been confirmed on this timeframe within the loaded history, or the level expired (Expire level input)."

sizeOf(string s) =>
    switch s
        "tiny"   => size.tiny
        "small"  => size.small
        "normal" => size.normal
        "large"  => size.large
        "huge"   => size.huge
        => size.normal

string lblSz = sizeOf(labelSize)
string tblSz = sizeOf(tblSize)

// Rows lower than the chart TF would only see the last intrabar of each chart
// bar; a row equal to the chart TF would be the Chart row one bar late (the
// engine runs on completed bars); a row that is not a whole multiple of the
// chart TF can differ between history and real time on the chart bar that
// straddles its close; tick charts have no time length to compare.
tfNote(simple string tf) =>
    int s = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    timeframe.isticks ? "tick chart" : s < chartSec ? "< chart" : s == chartSec ? "= chart" : s % chartSec != 0 ? "not a multiple" : ""

string n5S  = tfNote("5S")
string n10S = tfNote("10S")
string n15S = tfNote("15S")
string n30S = tfNote("30S")
string n1   = tfNote("1")
string n5   = tfNote("5")
string n15  = tfNote("15")
string n60  = tfNote("60")
string n240 = tfNote("240")
string nD   = tfNote("D")
string nW   = tfNote("W")
bool   v5S  = n5S == ""
bool   v10S = n10S == ""
bool   v15S = n15S == ""
bool   v30S = n30S == ""
bool   v1   = n1 == ""
bool   v5   = n5 == ""
bool   v15  = n15 == ""
bool   v60  = n60 == ""
bool   v240 = n240 == ""
bool   vD   = nD == ""
bool   vW   = nW == ""

// A row that is off or hidden is never read, so its request is pointed at the
// weekly series (a few hundred bars on any symbol) instead of loading and
// processing the full intraday history for nothing. All gates are simple, so
// each request runs on every bar or never, and the engine state stays consistent.
string tf5S  = use5S  and v5S  ? "5S"  : "W"
string tf10S = use10S and v10S ? "10S" : "W"
string tf15S = use15S and v15S ? "15S" : "W"
string tf30S = use30S and v30S ? "30S" : "W"
string tf1   = use1   and v1   ? "1"   : "W"
string tf5   = use5   and v5   ? "5"   : "W"
string tf15  = use15  and v15  ? "15"  : "W"
string tf60  = use60  and v60  ? "60"  : "W"
string tf240 = use240 and v240 ? "240" : "W"
string tfD   = useD   and vD   ? "D"   : "W"

// ── Chart TF ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool chartGate = not chartCloseOnly or barstate.isconfirmed
[cUpL, cDnL, cAtr, cUpHit, cDnHit, cUpAge, cDnAge, cUpT, cDnT, cUpB, cDnB, cN] = tfEngine(0, chartSec, chartGate)
// With bar-close gating the confirming tick is immediately followed by the next
// bar, so "Confirmed" is also shown on that next bar (cUpHit[1] is the committed
// closing value: identical on history and in real time).
int cUpSt = sideStage(cUpL, cAtr, cAtr, cUpHit or (chartCloseOnly and cUpHit[1]), cUpT, cUpB)
int cDnSt = sideStage(cDnL, cAtr, cAtr, cDnHit or (chartCloseOnly and cDnHit[1]), cDnT, cDnB)

plotshape(showMarks and bigMarks and cUpHit,     title = "Up fractal",         style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.abovebar, color = bullCol, size = size.normal, offset = -rightBars)
plotshape(showMarks and bigMarks and cDnHit,     title = "Dn fractal",         style = shape.triangledown, location = location.belowbar, color = bearCol, size = size.normal, offset = -rightBars)
plotshape(showMarks and not bigMarks and cUpHit, title = "Up fractal (small)", style = shape.triangleup,   location = location.abovebar, color = bullCol, size = size.tiny,   offset = -rightBars)
plotshape(showMarks and not bigMarks and cDnHit, title = "Dn fractal (small)", style = shape.triangledown, location = location.belowbar, color = bearCol, size = size.tiny,   offset = -rightBars)

// ── Higher TFs (completed bars only) ─────────────────────────────────────────
[u5S,  d5S,  a5S,  uh5S,  dh5S,  ua5S,  da5S,  ut5S,  dt5S,  ub5S,  db5S,  n5Sb]  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf5S,  tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf5S),  true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u10S, d10S, a10S, uh10S, dh10S, ua10S, da10S, ut10S, dt10S, ub10S, db10S, n10Sb] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf10S, tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf10S), true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u15S, d15S, a15S, uh15S, dh15S, ua15S, da15S, ut15S, dt15S, ub15S, db15S, n15Sb] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf15S, tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf15S), true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u30S, d30S, a30S, uh30S, dh30S, ua30S, da30S, ut30S, dt30S, ub30S, db30S, n30Sb] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf30S, tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf30S), true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u1,   d1,   a1,   uh1,   dh1,   ua1,   da1,   ut1,   dt1,   ub1,   db1,   n1b]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf1,   tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf1),   true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u5,   d5,   a5,   uh5,   dh5,   ua5,   da5,   ut5,   dt5,   ub5,   db5,   n5b]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf5,   tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf5),   true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u15,  d15,  a15,  uh15,  dh15,  ua15,  da15,  ut15,  dt15,  ub15,  db15,  n15b]  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf15,  tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf15),  true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u60,  d60,  a60,  uh60,  dh60,  ua60,  da60,  ut60,  dt60,  ub60,  db60,  n60b]  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf60,  tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf60),  true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[u240, d240, a240, uh240, dh240, ua240, da240, ut240, dt240, ub240, db240, n240b] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf240, tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tf240), true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[uD,   dD,   aD,   uhD,   dhD,   uaD,   daD,   utD,   dtD,   ubD,   dbD,   nDb]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tfD,   tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds(tfD),   true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[uW,   dW,   aW,   uhW,   dhW,   uaW,   daW,   utW,   dtW,   ubW,   dbW,   nWb]   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W",   tfEngine(1, timeframe.in_seconds("W"),   true), gaps = barmerge.gaps_off, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

int us5S  = sideStage(u5S,  a5S,  cAtr, uh5S,  ut5S,  ub5S)
int ds5S  = sideStage(d5S,  a5S,  cAtr, dh5S,  dt5S,  db5S)
int us10S = sideStage(u10S, a10S, cAtr, uh10S, ut10S, ub10S)
int ds10S = sideStage(d10S, a10S, cAtr, dh10S, dt10S, db10S)
int us15S = sideStage(u15S, a15S, cAtr, uh15S, ut15S, ub15S)
int ds15S = sideStage(d15S, a15S, cAtr, dh15S, dt15S, db15S)
int us30S = sideStage(u30S, a30S, cAtr, uh30S, ut30S, ub30S)
int ds30S = sideStage(d30S, a30S, cAtr, dh30S, dt30S, db30S)
int us1   = sideStage(u1,   a1,   cAtr, uh1,   ut1,   ub1)
int ds1   = sideStage(d1,   a1,   cAtr, dh1,   dt1,   db1)
int us5   = sideStage(u5,   a5,   cAtr, uh5,   ut5,   ub5)
int ds5   = sideStage(d5,   a5,   cAtr, dh5,   dt5,   db5)
int us15  = sideStage(u15,  a15,  cAtr, uh15,  ut15,  ub15)
int ds15  = sideStage(d15,  a15,  cAtr, dh15,  dt15,  db15)
int us60  = sideStage(u60,  a60,  cAtr, uh60,  ut60,  ub60)
int ds60  = sideStage(d60,  a60,  cAtr, dh60,  dt60,  db60)
int us240 = sideStage(u240, a240, cAtr, uh240, ut240, ub240)
int ds240 = sideStage(d240, a240, cAtr, dh240, dt240, db240)
int usD   = sideStage(uD,   aD,   cAtr, uhD,   utD,   ubD)
int dsD   = sideStage(dD,   aD,   cAtr, dhD,   dtD,   dbD)
int usW   = sideStage(uW,   aW,   cAtr, uhW,   utW,   ubW)
int dsW   = sideStage(dW,   aW,   cAtr, dhW,   dtW,   dbW)

// ── Row model ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
type Row
    string name
    bool   on
    bool   valid
    string note
    float  upL
    float  dnL
    float  atr
    int    upSt
    int    dnSt
    int    upAge
    int    dnAge
    int    upT
    int    dnT
    int    nBars

rows = array.new<Row>()
array.push(rows, Row.new("Chart", useChart, true, "",   cUpL, cDnL, cAtr, cUpSt, cDnSt, cUpAge, cDnAge, cUpT, cDnT, cN))
array.push(rows, Row.new("5s",    use5S,    v5S,  n5S,  u5S,  d5S,  a5S,  us5S,  ds5S,  ua5S,  da5S,  ut5S,  dt5S,  n5Sb))
array.push(rows, Row.new("10s",   use10S,   v10S, n10S, u10S, d10S, a10S, us10S, ds10S, ua10S, da10S, ut10S, dt10S, n10Sb))
array.push(rows, Row.new("15s",   use15S,   v15S, n15S, u15S, d15S, a15S, us15S, ds15S, ua15S, da15S, ut15S, dt15S, n15Sb))
array.push(rows, Row.new("30s",   use30S,   v30S, n30S, u30S, d30S, a30S, us30S, ds30S, ua30S, da30S, ut30S, dt30S, n30Sb))
array.push(rows, Row.new("1m",    use1,     v1,   n1,   u1,   d1,   a1,   us1,   ds1,   ua1,   da1,   ut1,   dt1,   n1b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("5m",    use5,     v5,   n5,   u5,   d5,   a5,   us5,   ds5,   ua5,   da5,   ut5,   dt5,   n5b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("15m",   use15,    v15,  n15,  u15,  d15,  a15,  us15,  ds15,  ua15,  da15,  ut15,  dt15,  n15b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("1H",    use60,    v60,  n60,  u60,  d60,  a60,  us60,  ds60,  ua60,  da60,  ut60,  dt60,  n60b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("4H",    use240,   v240, n240, u240, d240, a240, us240, ds240, ua240, da240, ut240, dt240, n240b))
array.push(rows, Row.new("D",     useD,     vD,   nD,   uD,   dD,   aD,   usD,   dsD,   uaD,   daD,   utD,   dtD,   nDb))
array.push(rows, Row.new("W",     useW,     vW,   nW,   uW,   dW,   aW,   usW,   dsW,   uaW,   daW,   utW,   dtW,   nWb))

// ── MTF bias ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// +1 per TF whose last swing HIGH is broken (price above resistance),
// −1 per TF whose last swing LOW is broken (price below support).
// Intact levels, Retest and Failed break contribute 0.
biasOf(int upS, int dnS) =>
    int b = 0
    if upS == 3 or upS == 5
        b += 1
    if dnS == 3 or dnS == 5
        b -= 1
    b

int    bias      = 0
int    nScore    = 0
int    nBelow    = 0
string hiddenTxt = ""
for r in rows
    if r.on and r.valid
        bias   += biasOf(r.upSt, r.dnSt)
        nScore += 1
    else if r.on
        if r.note == "< chart"
            nBelow += 1
        else
            hiddenTxt += (hiddenTxt == "" ? "" : ", ") + r.name + " (" + r.note + ")"
if nBelow > 0
    hiddenTxt := str.tostring(nBelow) + " row(s) below the chart TF" + (hiddenTxt == "" ? "" : ", " + hiddenTxt)

plot(bias, "MTF fractal bias", display = display.data_window)
bgcolor(showBiasBg and bias > 0 ? color.new(bullCol, 92) : showBiasBg and bias < 0 ? color.new(bearCol, 92) : na, title = "Bias tint")

// ── Stage table ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pos = switch tblPos
    "top_left"     => position.top_left
    "top_right"    => position.top_right
    "bottom_left"  => position.bottom_left
    => position.bottom_right
var table t = table.new(pos, 6, 14, bgcolor = color.new(#0d1117, 15), border_width = 1, border_color = color.new(color.gray, 60))

fmtPx(float x) =>
    na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(x, pxFmt)

bandText(float lvl, float atrV) =>
    float buf  = breakBuf(lvl, atrV)
    float band = math.max(retestBand(lvl, math.sqrt(atrV * cAtr)), buf)
    "ATR " + fmtPx(atrV) + "  ·  retest ±" + fmtPx(band) + "  ·  break buffer " + fmtPx(buf)

paintRow(int row, Row r) =>
    int b = biasOf(r.upSt, r.dnSt)
    bool tooShort = r.nBars < leftBars + rightBars + 1
    string shortTxt = "only " + str.tostring(r.nBars) + " bars"
    string ageNote  = r.name == "Chart" ? " bars" : " bars (as of last closed " + r.name + " bar)"
    string rowTip   = r.name == "Chart" ? (chartCloseOnly ? "The chart's own timeframe. Level and break state update on the bar close; Retest follows the live bar." : "The chart's own timeframe. Level and break state update intrabar ('Chart-TF signals on bar close only' is Off) and can change until the bar closes; Retest follows the live bar.") : "Levels and break state from completed " + r.name + " bars (no repainting); Retest follows the live chart bar."
    string noLvlTip = tooShort ? "Fewer completed bars than Bars left + Bars right + 1; a fractal cannot be confirmed yet." : stageDesc(0)
    table.cell(t, 0, row, r.name, text_color = color.silver, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = rowTip)
    table.cell(t, 1, row, fmtPx(r.upL), text_color = bullCol, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = na(r.upL) ? "" : "Last swing high (resistance)  ·  " + bandText(r.upL, r.atr) + "  ·  age " + str.tostring(r.upAge) + ageNote)
    table.cell(t, 2, row, na(r.upL) and tooShort ? shortTxt : stageName(r.upSt), text_color = stageColor(r.upSt), text_size = tblSz, tooltip = na(r.upL) ? noLvlTip : stageDesc(r.upSt))
    table.cell(t, 3, row, fmtPx(r.dnL), text_color = bearCol, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = na(r.dnL) ? "" : "Last swing low (support)  ·  " + bandText(r.dnL, r.atr) + "  ·  age " + str.tostring(r.dnAge) + ageNote)
    table.cell(t, 4, row, na(r.dnL) and tooShort ? shortTxt : stageName(r.dnSt), text_color = stageColor(r.dnSt), text_size = tblSz, tooltip = na(r.dnL) ? noLvlTip : stageDesc(r.dnSt))
    table.cell(t, 5, row, b > 0 ? "+1" : b < 0 ? "−1" : "0", text_color = b > 0 ? bullCol : b < 0 ? bearCol : color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "+1: swing high broken (price above resistance). −1: swing low broken (price below support). 0: both levels intact, or a failed break.")

if showStageTbl and barstate.islast
    table.cell(t, 0, 0, "TF",       text_color = color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "Timeframe of the row. Rows below the chart timeframe, equal to it, or not a whole multiple of it are hidden.")
    table.cell(t, 1, 0, "Swing hi", text_color = color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "Last confirmed swing high of that timeframe: resistance until broken.")
    table.cell(t, 2, 0, "Stage",    text_color = color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "Confirmed · Holding · Retest · Broken · Flip retest · Failed break. Hover a stage for its meaning.")
    table.cell(t, 3, 0, "Swing lo", text_color = color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "Last confirmed swing low of that timeframe: support until broken.")
    table.cell(t, 4, 0, "Stage",    text_color = color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "Confirmed · Holding · Retest · Broken · Flip retest · Failed break. Hover a stage for its meaning.")
    table.cell(t, 5, 0, "Bias",     text_color = color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "+1 broken swing high, −1 broken swing low, 0 otherwise. The Σ row sums the visible rows.")
    int rowIdx = 1
    for r in rows
        if r.on and r.valid
            paintRow(rowIdx, r)
            rowIdx += 1
    string profTxt = resolved + (rollOn ? " · rollover filter" : "") + "  L" + str.tostring(leftBars) + "/R" + str.tostring(rightBars) + (useAtrBand ? "  ATR" + str.tostring(atrLen) + " ×" + str.tostring(retestMul) + "/" + str.tostring(breakMul) : "  " + str.tostring(retestPct) + "%/" + str.tostring(breakPct) + "%")
    string sumTip  = "Sum of the per-TF bias over the enabled, usable timeframes (bias / rows counted). Positive: more timeframes have broken above resistance than below support." + (hiddenTxt == "" ? "" : "  Hidden: " + hiddenTxt + ". A row must be higher than the chart timeframe and a whole multiple of it; the Chart row covers the chart timeframe.")
    table.cell(t, 0, rowIdx, "Σ", text_color = color.gray, text_size = tblSz)
    table.cell(t, 1, rowIdx, profTxt, text_color = color.silver, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = "Symbol profile" + (rollOn ? " (rollover filter on)" : "") + " · fractal left/right · " + (useAtrBand ? "ATR length × retest multiplier / break multiplier" : "retest band % / break buffer % (Percent mode)"))
    table.cell(t, 2, rowIdx, "", text_size = tblSz)
    table.cell(t, 3, rowIdx, "", text_size = tblSz)
    table.cell(t, 4, rowIdx, "", text_size = tblSz)
    table.cell(t, 5, rowIdx, (bias > 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(bias) + " / " + str.tostring(nScore), text_color = bias > 0 ? bullCol : bias < 0 ? bearCol : color.gray, text_size = tblSz, tooltip = sumTip)

// ── Labels on last chart fractals ────────────────────────────────────────────
var label upLab = na
var label dnLab = na
if showLabels and barstate.islast
    label.delete(upLab)
    label.delete(dnLab)
    if not na(cUpL)
        upLab := label.new(bar_index + 1, cUpL, "▲ Swing high " + fmtPx(cUpL) + "\n" + stageName(cUpSt) + " · " + str.tostring(cUpAge) + " bars", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(bullCol, 75), textcolor = bullCol, size = lblSz, tooltip = stageDesc(cUpSt) + "\n" + bandText(cUpL, cAtr))
    if not na(cDnL)
        dnLab := label.new(bar_index + 1, cDnL, "▼ Swing low " + fmtPx(cDnL) + "\n" + stageName(cDnSt) + " · " + str.tostring(cDnAge) + " bars", xloc = xloc.bar_index, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(bearCol, 75), textcolor = bearCol, size = lblSz, tooltip = stageDesc(cDnSt) + "\n" + bandText(cDnL, cAtr))

// ── Level lines ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var line cUpLine = na
var line cDnLine = na
if showLines and barstate.islast
    line.delete(cUpLine)
    line.delete(cDnLine)
    if not na(cUpL) and not na(cUpT)
        cUpLine := line.new(cUpT, cUpL, time + chartSec * 1000, cUpL, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(bullCol, 30), style = line.style_solid, width = 1)
    if not na(cDnL) and not na(cDnT)
        cDnLine := line.new(cDnT, cDnL, time + chartSec * 1000, cDnL, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(bearCol, 30), style = line.style_solid, width = 1)

// Higher-TF lines start at the open time of the fractal's centre bar.
var array<line> htfLines = array.new<line>()
if showHtfLines and barstate.islast
    for l in htfLines
        line.delete(l)
    array.clear(htfLines)
    int tEnd = time + chartSec * 1000 * 2
    for r in rows
        if r.on and r.valid and r.name != "Chart"
            if not na(r.upL) and not na(r.upT)
                array.push(htfLines, line.new(r.upT, r.upL, tEnd, r.upL, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(bullCol, 55), style = line.style_dashed, width = 1))
            if not na(r.dnL) and not na(r.dnT)
                array.push(htfLines, line.new(r.dnT, r.dnL, tEnd, r.dnL, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color.new(bearCol, 55), style = line.style_dashed, width = 1))

// ── Alerts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every helper is evaluated unconditionally at global scope so its [1] history
// is complete (v6 and/or short-circuit would otherwise skip calls).
enteredBroken(int st) =>
    (st == 3 or st == 5) and not (st[1] == 3 or st[1] == 5)
enteredRetest(int st) =>
    (st == 2 or st == 5) and not (st[1] == 2 or st[1] == 5)

bool cUpBrk = enteredBroken(cUpSt) and chartGate
bool cDnBrk = enteredBroken(cDnSt) and chartGate
bool cUpRt  = enteredRetest(cUpSt)
bool cDnRt  = enteredRetest(cDnSt)
bool b5Su   = enteredBroken(us5S)
bool b5Sd   = enteredBroken(ds5S)
bool b10Su  = enteredBroken(us10S)
bool b10Sd  = enteredBroken(ds10S)
bool b15Su  = enteredBroken(us15S)
bool b15Sd  = enteredBroken(ds15S)
bool b30Su  = enteredBroken(us30S)
bool b30Sd  = enteredBroken(ds30S)
bool b1u    = enteredBroken(us1)
bool b1d    = enteredBroken(ds1)
bool b5u    = enteredBroken(us5)
bool b5d    = enteredBroken(ds5)
bool b15u   = enteredBroken(us15)
bool b15d   = enteredBroken(ds15)
bool b60u   = enteredBroken(us60)
bool b60d   = enteredBroken(ds60)
bool b240u  = enteredBroken(us240)
bool b240d  = enteredBroken(ds240)
bool bDu    = enteredBroken(usD)
bool bDd    = enteredBroken(dsD)
bool bWu    = enteredBroken(usW)
bool bWd    = enteredBroken(dsW)

bool htfUpBreak = (use5S and v5S and b5Su) or (use10S and v10S and b10Su) or (use15S and v15S and b15Su) or (use30S and v30S and b30Su) or (use1 and v1 and b1u) or (use5 and v5 and b5u) or (use15 and v15 and b15u) or (use60 and v60 and b60u) or (use240 and v240 and b240u) or (useD and vD and bDu) or (useW and vW and bWu)
bool htfDnBreak = (use5S and v5S and b5Sd) or (use10S and v10S and b10Sd) or (use15S and v15S and b15Sd) or (use30S and v30S and b30Sd) or (use1 and v1 and b1d) or (use5 and v5 and b5d) or (use15 and v15 and b15d) or (use60 and v60 and b60d) or (use240 and v240 and b240d) or (useD and vD and bDd) or (useW and vW and bWd)

// Strategies cannot create alertcondition() alerts; the order fills carry
// alert messages instead (Strategy alert in the alert dialog).

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Strategy
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
string G_STRAT = "Strategy entries"
string G_RISK  = "Risk and exits"

dirMode   = input.string("Both", "Direction", options = ["Both", "Long only", "Short only"], group = G_STRAT)
useBreak  = input.bool(true, "Enter on chart-TF swing break", group = G_STRAT,
     tooltip = "Long when the chart-TF swing high turns Broken (close above the level by more than the buffer), short when the swing low turns Broken. Fires on the bar close.")
useFlip   = input.bool(true, "Enter on flip retest", group = G_STRAT,
     tooltip = "Long when the chart-TF swing high is in Flip retest (broken earlier, price back at it from above) and the bar closes above the level; short mirrored on the swing low. One entry per level.")
biasMin   = input.int(0, "Min higher-TF bias in trade direction", minval = 0, maxval = 11, group = G_STRAT,
     tooltip = "Sum of the bias of the visible higher-TF rows (Chart row excluded). Longs need bias >= this value, shorts need bias <= minus this value. 0 = higher timeframes must not be against the trade; 1 = at least one higher timeframe must already have broken in the trade direction.")
allowRev  = input.bool(false, "Allow reversal (opposite signal flips the position)", group = G_STRAT)
exitOnOpp = input.bool(true, "Exit when the opposite chart-TF swing breaks", group = G_STRAT,
     tooltip = "Close a long when the chart-TF swing low turns Broken, a short when the swing high turns Broken.")
maxBars   = input.int(0, "Time stop: close after N bars (0 = off)", minval = 0, group = G_STRAT)
sessIn    = input.session("0000-0000", "Trading session (exchange time)", group = G_STRAT,
     tooltip = "Entries only inside this session. 0000-0000 = always. Exits are always active.")
startDate = input.time(timestamp("2024-01-01T00:00:00"), "Backtest start", group = G_STRAT)
endDate   = input.time(timestamp("2030-12-31T00:00:00"), "Backtest end",   group = G_STRAT)

stopMode  = input.string("ATR", "Stop placement", options = ["ATR", "Structure"], group = G_RISK,
     tooltip = "ATR: entry minus the stop distance below. Structure: for a breakout, beyond the opposite chart-TF swing (last swing low for a long) plus the break buffer; for a flip retest, beyond the retested level plus the buffer. Falls back to ATR when no structure level exists or it is on the wrong side of the entry.")
stopAtr   = input.float(1.5, "Stop distance (× chart ATR)", minval = 0.25, maxval = 10, step = 0.25, group = G_RISK,
     tooltip = "1.5 × ATR: about $20 on 1H gold, $780 on 1H BTC. Wide enough to survive the noise that the retest band tolerates (0.5 ATR) plus a push through it.")
rrTarget  = input.float(2.0, "Target (R multiple, 0 = none)", minval = 0, maxval = 20, step = 0.25, group = G_RISK)
beR       = input.float(1.0, "Move stop to breakeven at (R, 0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 10, step = 0.25, group = G_RISK)
trailAtr  = input.float(0.0, "ATR trailing stop (× chart ATR, 0 = off)", minval = 0, maxval = 10, step = 0.25, group = G_RISK)
riskPct   = input.float(1.0, "Risk per trade (% of equity)", minval = 0.05, maxval = 10, step = 0.05, group = G_RISK,
     tooltip = "Position size = equity × risk % ÷ stop distance, in units of the symbol (ounces, BTC). The same 1 % means the same account risk on gold and on bitcoin.")

// ── Filters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Higher-TF bias only: the chart row's own break is the trigger, not the filter.
int  htfBias = bias - (useChart ? biasOf(cUpSt, cDnSt) : 0)
bool inRange = time >= startDate and time <= endDate
bool inSess  = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessIn))

// Same rollover window as the fractal filter, applied to the chart bar.
string chartRollSess = chartSec >= 3600 ? "1600-1820:1234567" : chartSec >= 1800 ? "1630-1820:1234567" : "1640-1820:1234567"
int    chartRollT    = na
if rollOn and chartSec <= 3600 and not timeframe.isticks
    chartRollT := time(timeframe.period, chartRollSess, "America/New_York")
bool   chartRoll     = not na(chartRollT)

bool flat     = strategy.position_size == 0
bool canEnter = inRange and inSess and not chartRoll
bool canLong  = canEnter and dirMode != "Short only" and (flat or (allowRev and strategy.position_size < 0))
bool canShort = canEnter and dirMode != "Long only"  and (flat or (allowRev and strategy.position_size > 0))

// ── Signals ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var int lastFlipUpT = na
var int lastFlipDnT = na

bool longBreak  = useBreak and cUpBrk and htfBias >= biasMin
bool shortBreak = useBreak and cDnBrk and htfBias <= -biasMin
bool longFlip   = useFlip and cUpSt == 5 and close > cUpL and htfBias >= biasMin and (na(lastFlipUpT) or cUpT != lastFlipUpT)
bool shortFlip  = useFlip and cDnSt == 5 and close < cDnL and htfBias <= -biasMin and (na(lastFlipDnT) or cDnT != lastFlipDnT)

// ── Stops and sizing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
longStopFor(bool isBreak) =>
    float atrStop   = close - stopAtr * cAtr
    float structLvl = isBreak ? cDnL : cUpL
    float structStp = na(structLvl) ? na : structLvl - breakBuf(structLvl, cAtr)
    stopMode == "Structure" and not na(structStp) and structStp < close ? structStp : atrStop

shortStopFor(bool isBreak) =>
    float atrStop   = close + stopAtr * cAtr
    float structLvl = isBreak ? cUpL : cDnL
    float structStp = na(structLvl) ? na : structLvl + breakBuf(structLvl, cAtr)
    stopMode == "Structure" and not na(structStp) and structStp > close ? structStp : atrStop

float riskCash = strategy.equity * riskPct / 100.0

qtyFor(float stopDist) =>
    stopDist > 0 and riskCash > 0 ? riskCash / stopDist : na

var float lStop = na
var float lTp   = na
var float lRisk = na
var float sStop = na
var float sTp   = na
var float sRisk = na
var int   entryBar = na

// ── Entries ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if canLong and (longBreak or longFlip)
    float st   = longStopFor(longBreak)
    float dist = close - st
    float q    = qtyFor(dist)
    if not na(q) and q > 0
        lStop    := st
        lRisk    := dist
        lTp      := rrTarget > 0 ? close + rrTarget * dist : na
        entryBar := bar_index
        if longFlip and not longBreak
            lastFlipUpT := cUpT
        strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty = q, comment = longBreak ? "L break" : "L flip", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: LONG {{ticker}} at {{close}}")
        strategy.exit("L-X", "L", stop = lStop, limit = lTp, comment_loss = "L stop", comment_profit = "L target", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: long exit {{ticker}} at {{close}}")

if canShort and (shortBreak or shortFlip)
    float st   = shortStopFor(shortBreak)
    float dist = st - close
    float q    = qtyFor(dist)
    if not na(q) and q > 0
        sStop    := st
        sRisk    := dist
        sTp      := rrTarget > 0 ? close - rrTarget * dist : na
        entryBar := bar_index
        if shortFlip and not shortBreak
            lastFlipDnT := cDnT
        strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty = q, comment = shortBreak ? "S break" : "S flip", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: SHORT {{ticker}} at {{close}}")
        strategy.exit("S-X", "S", stop = sStop, limit = sTp, comment_loss = "S stop", comment_profit = "S target", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: short exit {{ticker}} at {{close}}")

// ── Exit management while in a position ──────────────────────────────────────
if strategy.position_size > 0
    float ep = strategy.position_avg_price
    if beR > 0 and not na(lRisk) and high >= ep + beR * lRisk
        lStop := math.max(lStop, ep)
    if trailAtr > 0
        lStop := math.max(lStop, close - trailAtr * cAtr)
    strategy.exit("L-X", "L", stop = lStop, limit = lTp, comment_loss = "L stop", comment_profit = "L target", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: long exit {{ticker}} at {{close}}")
    bool oppL  = exitOnOpp and cDnBrk
    bool timeL = maxBars > 0 and not na(entryBar) and bar_index - entryBar >= maxBars
    if oppL or timeL
        strategy.close("L", comment = oppL ? "L opp break" : "L time", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: long closed {{ticker}} at {{close}}")

if strategy.position_size < 0
    float ep = strategy.position_avg_price
    if beR > 0 and not na(sRisk) and low <= ep - beR * sRisk
        sStop := math.min(sStop, ep)
    if trailAtr > 0
        sStop := math.min(sStop, close + trailAtr * cAtr)
    strategy.exit("S-X", "S", stop = sStop, limit = sTp, comment_loss = "S stop", comment_profit = "S target", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: short exit {{ticker}} at {{close}}")
    bool oppS  = exitOnOpp and cUpBrk
    bool timeS = maxBars > 0 and not na(entryBar) and bar_index - entryBar >= maxBars
    if oppS or timeS
        strategy.close("S", comment = oppS ? "S opp break" : "S time", alert_message = "MTF Fractals: short closed {{ticker}} at {{close}}")

// ── Stop / target lines while in a trade ─────────────────────────────────────
plot(strategy.position_size > 0 ? lStop : na, "Long stop",    color = color.new(color.red, 0),   style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(strategy.position_size > 0 ? lTp   : na, "Long target",  color = color.new(color.green, 0), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(strategy.position_size < 0 ? sStop : na, "Short stop",   color = color.new(color.red, 0),   style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(strategy.position_size < 0 ? sTp   : na, "Short target", color = color.new(color.green, 0), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
